title: Karl Radek
is-pinned-card: true
tags: advisor
view-if: adv_show_radek = 1
new-page: true

= Karl Radek

The Comintern's man for Germany: born in Lemberg, a brilliant journalist, a wit, and a conspirator who has been expelled from more parties than most men have joined. He speaks for Moscow, and he changes his mind as often as Moscow does.

- @money
- @report
- @root: Return to main

@money
title: Ask Radek for Money
subtitle: 3 funds. Moscow will expect to be heard.
unavailable-subtitle: [? if advisor_action_timer = 1 : Next advisor action in 1 month. ?][? if advisor_action_timer > 1 : Next advisor action in [+ advisor_action_timer +] months. ?]
choose-if: advisor_action_timer <= 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.advisor_action_timer = 5;
Q.last_advisor_action = 1;
Q.resources += 3;
Q.independence -= 6;
!}

Radek produces the money with a joke about capitalist banks. He is also taking notes.

@report
title: Let Radek Write the Report
subtitle: [? if lock_moscow_orders = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] He tells the Executive the directive is being carried out.
unavailable-subtitle: [? if advisor_action_timer = 1 : Next advisor action in 1 month. ?][? if advisor_action_timer > 1 : Next advisor action in [+ advisor_action_timer +] months. ?][? if directive_active = 0 : There is no directive from Moscow to report on. ?][? if lock_moscow_orders = 2 : The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids taking orders from Moscow. ?]
choose-if: advisor_action_timer <= 0 and directive_active = 1 and lock_moscow_orders < 2
on-arrival: {!
Q.advisor_action_timer = 4;
Q.last_advisor_action = 1;
if (Q.lock_moscow_orders == 1) {
    Q.unity -= 10;
    Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10;
}
RG.comply(20);
Q.independence -= 3;
!}

Radek writes the report on the directive himself, in his own style, with figures that are mostly true. The Executive is satisfied for now.
